# .trivyignore — the ONLY CVE escape hatch for the L4 security gate (Story 14.4 / ISI-2245, §6.2).
#
# This file is reviewed like code. Every suppression MUST carry, on the comment line directly
# above the CVE id:
#     <CVE-ID>   expires:YYYY-MM-DD   justification:<one line why this is accepted>
#
# The security.yml "trivyignore expiry lint" step FAILS the build when an entry is past its
# `expires:` date — a suppression is never a silent, perpetual mute. Remove or re-justify it
# before it expires. An unfixable finding still needs an entry (Trivy runs --ignore-unfixed, but
# a fix landing upstream turns a previously-unfixable HIGH into a gating one, so track it here).
#
# Format reference: https://trivy.dev/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/#trivyignore
#
# --- ISI-6822 fleet renewal 2026-10-29 (was: all 71 entries expired 2026-10-28 together) ---
# Full re-verification sweep, evidence per entry below. Upstream checks + `trivy rootfs` on the
# candidate binaries + `trivy image` on the bases (DB 2026-10-29):
#   DELETED (15) — fixes verified landed:
#     oras-go 2.6.1 CVEs (50163/85731): helm v3.22.1 vendors oras-go 2.6.2, trivy-clean.
#     x/mod CVEs (56864/56865): gh v2.103.3 vendors x/mod 0.41.0, trivy-clean.
#     npm bundled CVEs (14257/69152/69192/73566): npm 12.2.1 bundles brace-expansion 5.0.12,
#       ip-address 10.7.2, node-tar 7.5.22 — verified from the 12.2.1 tarball; pin re-pinned.
#     util-linux CVEs (53612/53613/53614/76642/78408/78409/78410): python:3.12-alpine rebased
#       onto alpine 3.24.3 shipping util-linux 2.42.3-r1 — trivy image scan clean 2026-10-29.
#   PIN BUMPS in the same PR (fixes verified in-binary via go buildinfo + trivy):
#     helm v3.21.4→v3.22.1 (go1.26.9, x/net 0.60.0, oras 2.6.2), kubectl v1.36.4→v1.36.6
#     (go1.26.10), gh v2.98.0→v2.103.3 (go1.27.3, grpc 1.84.0), dtctl v0.38.0→v0.45.0
#     (go1.26.10, grpc 1.83.2), npm 12.0.2→12.2.1; docker-cli apk pass +brotli-libs +libcurl.
#   NEW (4) — advisories the 2026-10 DB added against still-shipping versions: 111943, 56851,
#     56857, GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf.
#   STAGGER: expiry dates are now split per carrier group (11-12 runtime bases / 11-19
#     clusterctl / 11-26 kubectl+docker-cli) so the fleet can never expire as one batch again.
#
# --- active suppressions ---
# openssl CVE batch in the ksquad-console RUNTIME base (gcr.io/distroless/nodejs24-debian12:nonroot,
# libssl3 3.0.18-1~deb12u2, debian 12.13). Fixes exist upstream (libssl3 3.0.19/3.0.20-1~deb12u2 in
# bookworm security) and ride the next distroless tag rebuild; distroless has no package manager so
# the image cannot be patched in-repo. Remediation is external (upstream distroless base rebuild) —
# there is no open in-repo ticket: origin was ISI-2852 (done), renewal cadence is ISI-4695.
# Re-verified 2026-10-08 (ISI-4695 cadence): base pin UNCHANGED, no rebuild adopted in-repo.
# Re-verified 2026-10-29 (ISI-6822): inspected the live nonroot manifest dpkg status.d + trivy
# image scan — the base STILL ships libssl3 3.0.18-1~deb12u2 (fixes 3.0.19/3.0.20-1~deb12u2),
# so the distroless rebuild STILL has not landed and every CVE below remains present and
# unpatchable-in-repo. Renewed (not blind).
# CVE-2026-31789   expires:2026-11-12   justification:CRITICAL openssl heap overflow (32-bit X.509); runtime-base-only, patch pending distroless rebuild of nodejs24-debian12 (re-verified 2026-10-29: base still libssl3 3.0.18)
CVE-2026-31789
